{"case_id":"T5031","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","attack_surface"],"commit_induced":"NO","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["spng_encode_image","write_idat_bytes"],"reason":"H0 exercises PNG decoding through spng_decoded_image_size, spng_decode_image, and spng_decode_row, but never invokes the encoder entry point spng_encode_image. Therefore S1's changed IDAT-writing behavior is unreachable. However, the same encoder-coverage gap already existed in S0, so this commit neither introduced nor materially aggravated it.","evidence":["tests/spng_read_fuzzer.c creates a context and calls decoder APIs, including spng_decoded_image_size(), spng_decode_image(), and spng_decode_row().","No H0 path calls spng_encode_image(), encode_row(), or write_idat_bytes().","Both S0 and S1 contain the same public spng_encode_image(spng_ctx *ctx, const void *img, size_t len, int fmt, int flags) entry point, and H0 reaches it in neither snapshot.","The diff changes encoder-internal IDAT initialization and state handling: spng_encode_image() now calls write_header(), initializes zstream->avail_out/next_out, and sets ctx->state = SPNG_STATE_FIRST_IDAT; write_idat_bytes() removes its prior first-IDAT initialization block."],"recommended_action":"No commit-specific harness maintenance is required. Encoder fuzzing could be added as independent coverage improvement, but it addresses a pre-existing gap rather than one caused by this commit."}
